# Milestone: v0.9.4 (originally drafted at M3; reactivated at Phase 5 Task 5.4)
# Covers: every() installed inside an ambient tag scope (mytag: { ... })
#         survives the scope unwind and continues firing.  The tag prefix
#         pushes a UTag onto the cleanup stack at OP_PUSH_TAG and pops it at
#         OP_POP_TAG; the every() call captures the innermost user-tag at
#         install time via periodic_alloc -> innermost_user_tag.
#
# Reduced scope vs. the original M3 draft: the original intent was
# `t: every(P) X; t.stop()` — assert that t.stop() cancels the periodic.
# That requires Tag.new() (scripted UTag constructor) so the identifier `t`
# resolves to a real UTag with a .stop() method.  Tag.new() is still v1.x-
# deferred (see tests/chk/reactive/tag/{tag_enter,tag_leave}.chk).
#
# Today the tag identifier resolves to nil and the tag-scope creates an
# anonymous UTag bound only to the cleanup stack — no urbiscript handle.
# Cancellation by user-tag from urbiscript is therefore still blocked.
# What IS testable now: that wrapping every() in a tag scope does not
# disturb periodic install or firing.  Asserted below by counter check.
#
# When Tag.new() lands (v1.x), restore the original `t: every(P) X; t.stop()`
# form and assert the periodic stops firing after .stop().

var fired = 0
var heartbeat = nil
heartbeat: { every (1us) Realm.fired = Realm.fired + 1 }
0
0
Realm.fired > 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] true
